{% macro task_analysis(activities, duration_minutes, activity_count, start_time, end_time, primary_category, primary_project, accomplishment_count) -%}
ACTIVITIES:
{{ activities }}

METADATA:
- Project: {{ primary_project }}
- Duration: {{ duration_minutes }} minutes
- Activity count: {{ activity_count }}
- Time range: {{ start_time }} to {{ end_time }}
- Primary category: {{ primary_category }}

Rules:
- All events belong to project "{{ primary_project }}". If other project names appear in the log, that is a data artefact — treat everything as the same project.
- NEVER group multiple events into one vague item. Each accomplishment must correspond to a specific, individual event.
- NEVER write category descriptions. BAD: "Explored music videos on YouTube". GOOD: "Watched 'Kendrick Lamar - Not Like Us' on YouTube". BAD: "Ran several echo commands". GOOD: "Ran: echo 'hello world', echo $PATH, echo -e '\t tab test'".
- NEVER use filler phrases: "maintained productive workflow", "continued working", "completed activities", "engaged in tasks", "focused on development", "explored various", "performed multiple".
- For screen/accessibility events with conversation text: note who said what and the topic. BAD: "Had a conversation in Claude". GOOD: "Claude chat: asked about HDBSCAN min_cluster_size, Claude explained epsilon parameter".
- For git/terminal: use the exact command, branch, commit message, filenames verbatim from the log.
- For browser: use the exact page title and domain from the log.

Provide:

1. TASK_TITLE: Specific title (max 50 chars). Include the project or tool name and a concrete action. Examples: "patcha-3: fix event dedup in compaction.py", "Claude chat: debug HDBSCAN clustering", "YouTube: Kendrick Lamar & Tyler the Creator videos".

2. ACCOMPLISHMENTS: List up to {{ accomplishment_count }} items — one per distinct event or action. Use the exact names, commands, titles, and URLs from the activity log above. If there are fewer distinct events than {{ accomplishment_count }}, list fewer items.

3. DESCRIPTION: One sentence. Name the project, what specifically was done, and the outcome or purpose.

4. MAIN_THEMES: 2-3 short keywords from the actual content — tool names, artist names, project subsystems. No generic terms.

Format:
TASK_TITLE: [title]
ACCOMPLISHMENTS:
- [item 1]
- [item 2]
- [item 3]
DESCRIPTION: [one sentence]
MAIN_THEMES: [theme1, theme2, theme3]
{%- endmacro %}


{% macro task_enhance(activities_text, project, category, duration_minutes, activity_count) -%}
Activities:
{{ activities_text }}

Project: {{ project }}
Category: {{ category }}
Duration: {{ duration_minutes }} minutes
Activity count: {{ activity_count }}

Provide:
TITLE: concise descriptive title (max 60 chars)
DESCRIPTION: 1-2 sentences on what this task involved
PRIORITY: low/medium/high/urgent
CONFIDENCE: 0.0-1.0 score for how well these activities form a coherent task
{%- endmacro %}


{% macro category_summary(category_name, event_count, summaries, extra_count) -%}
Summarize the following {{ category_name }} activities from today in 2-4 sentences. Focus on accomplishments and patterns.

Activities ({{ event_count }} total):
{% for s in summaries -%}
- {{ s }}
{% endfor -%}
{%- if extra_count > 0 %}
... and {{ extra_count }} more activities
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}


{% macro overall_summary(date_str, total_events, top_categories_str, projects_str) -%}
Summarize {{ date_str }} in 2-3 sentences covering productivity and focus areas.

Total activities: {{ total_events }}
Top categories: {{ top_categories_str }}
Projects: {{ projects_str }}
{%- endmacro %}


{% macro hourly_summary(hour_label, app_list, event_count, summaries) -%}
You are summarizing one hour of someone's computer activity for a timeline view.

Hour: {{ hour_label }}
Apps used: {{ app_list }}
Activity count: {{ event_count }}

Raw activity log:
{% for s in summaries -%}
- {{ s }}
{% endfor -%}

Write a concise summary of what the person worked on this hour. Then break the
work into a small task tree (root task -> sub-tasks -> concrete actions), using
the exact tools, files, commands, and topics from the log. Keep tree labels
short (max ~6 words). 2-4 children at the root; nest one level deeper only when
the log clearly supports it.

Respond with ONLY a JSON object, no markdown fences, in exactly this shape:
{
  "title": "short title, max 50 chars",
  "narrative": "1-2 sentence summary of the hour",
  "tree": {
    "label": "root task",
    "children": [
      { "label": "sub-task", "children": [ { "label": "action" } ] },
      { "label": "sub-task" }
    ]
  }
}
{%- endmacro %}


